Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Dan Frawley (1882–1967) was a pioneer Australian rugby league footballer, a national representative player.","title":"Dan Frawley"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He played his career as a winger with the Eastern Suburbs club in Sydney and is considered one of the nation's finest footballers of the 20th century.","title":"Dan Frawley"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" A fast and agile winger, with an ability to effortlessly change direction, Frawley was at club and representative levels generally positioned on the outside of rugby league Immortal Dally Messenger, creating a formidable combination.","title":"Dan Frawley"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" He was a noted speedster who, on the 1908–09 Kangaroo tour of Great Britain, was acclaimed as the \"100 yards champion\" of the squad.","title":"Dan Frawley"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Philadelphia Arrows were a professional ice hockey team that played in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.","title":"Philadelphia Arrows"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Founded in 1927, the club was Philadelphia's first professional hockey team and played in the Canadian-American Hockey League.","title":"Philadelphia Arrows"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The team changed its name to the Philadelphia Ramblers beginning with the 1935-36 season when it became affiliated with the NHL New York Rangers.","title":"Philadelphia Arrows"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The following season and Ramblers and the C-AHL began playing an interlocking schedule with the International Hockey League for two seasons before the two circuits formally merged to form a new International American Hockey League (renamed the American Hockey League in 1940) in June, 1938.","title":"Philadelphia Arrows"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" (The Ramblers continued to play in this league until folding in 1941.)","title":"Philadelphia Arrows"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Carter Bancks (born August 9, 1989) is a Canadian professional ice hockey player who is currently playing with and serving as captain of the Utica Comets of the American Hockey League (AHL).","title":"Carter Bancks"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He played the 2013–14 season under contract to with the Calgary Flames of the National Hockey League (NHL).","title":"Carter Bancks"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" An undrafted player, Bancks played four seasons of junior in the Western Hockey League (WHL) and four more in the American Hockey League (AHL) before making his NHL debut in 2013.","title":"Carter Bancks"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Bancks was born in Calgary, Alberta, but grew up in Marysville, British Columbia","title":"Carter Bancks"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Robert James Sullivan (born November 29, 1957) is a retired professional ice hockey player who played 62 games in the National Hockey League.","title":"Bob Sullivan (ice hockey)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He played for the Hartford Whalers.","title":"Bob Sullivan (ice hockey)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Prior to joining the NHL, Sullivan played in the American Hockey League and International Hockey League, winning the Dudley \"Red\" Garrett Memorial Award as the rookie of the year in the American Hockey League in 1981–82.","title":"Bob Sullivan (ice hockey)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Bryan Berry Helmer (born July 15, 1972) is a former professional ice hockey player.","title":"Bryan Helmer"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is currently the VP of Hockey Operations with the Hershey Bears of the American Hockey League (AHL).","title":"Bryan Helmer"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" He previously served as an assistant coach with the Bears and the Peterborough Petes of the Ontario Hockey League (OHL).","title":"Bryan Helmer"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" A veteran of over 1,000 AHL and IHL games, Helmer previously served as captain for the Hershey Bears in the American Hockey League (AHL).","title":"Bryan Helmer"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" He has also played in the National Hockey League (NHL) with the Phoenix Coyotes, St. Louis Blues, Vancouver Canucks and the Washington Capitals.","title":"Bryan Helmer"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Marcel Cousineau (born April 30, 1973) is a retired professional ice hockey player who played 26 games in the National Hockey League.","title":"Marcel Cousineau"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was selected by Boston Bruins in third round of the NHL draft.","title":"Marcel Cousineau"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" As a rookie, he was named to the Quebec Major Junior Hockey League All-Rookie Team.","title":"Marcel Cousineau"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" He also played professionally for the Toronto Maple Leafs (1996–98), New York Islanders (1998–99), Los Angeles Kings (1999-2000).","title":"Marcel Cousineau"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Between his starts in the NHL he played stints in the minors (American Hockey League, International Hockey League, Quebec Senior Hockey League, Ligue Nord-Américaine de Hockey) and overseas Russia (Kontinental Hockey League):","title":"Marcel Cousineau"}

