Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Brooklyn Danielle Decker Roddick (born April 12, 1987) is an American fashion model and actress best known for her appearances in the \"Sports Illustrated Swimsuit Issue\", including the cover of the 2010 issue.","title":"Brooklyn Decker"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" In addition to working for Victoria's Secret for the 2010 \"Swim\" collection, she has ventured into television with guest appearances on \"Chuck\", \"Ugly Betty\", \"The League\", and \"Royal Pains\".","title":"Brooklyn Decker"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" She made her feature film debut in \"Just Go with It\", and later starred in \"Battleship\" and \"What to Expect When You're Expecting\".","title":"Brooklyn Decker"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Decker is married to former tennis player Andy Roddick.","title":"Brooklyn Decker"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Andy Roddick was the defending champion and won in the final 7–6, 7–6 against Ivo Karlović.","title":"2005 Stella Artois Championships – Singles"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" This was the first ATP tournament of future World No. 1 Andy Murray in his professional debut.","title":"2005 Stella Artois Championships – Singles"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"This is a list of the main career statistics of retired professional American tennis player, Andy Roddick.","title":"Andy Roddick career statistics"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Throughout his career, Roddick won thirty-two ATP singles titles including one grand slam singles title and five ATP Masters 1000 singles titles.","title":"Andy Roddick career statistics"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" He was also the runner-up at the Wimbledon Championships in 2004, 2005 and 2009 and the US Open in 2006, losing on all four occasions to Roger Federer.","title":"Andy Roddick career statistics"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Roddick was also a four-time semi-finalist at the Australian Open and a three-time semi-finalist at the year-ending ATP World Tour Finals.","title":"Andy Roddick career statistics"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" On November 3, 2003, Roddick became the World No. 1 for the first time in his career.","title":"Andy Roddick career statistics"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Janko Tipsarević (, ] ; born 22 June 1984) is a Serbian professional tennis player.","title":"Janko Tipsarević"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" His career-high singles ranking is world No. 8, achieved on 2 April 2012.","title":"Janko Tipsarević"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" In his career, he has won four ATP World Tour titles, one ATP doubles title, three Futures, and 15 Challenger titles.","title":"Janko Tipsarević"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Tipsarević also won the 2001 Australian Open Junior title.","title":"Janko Tipsarević"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Tipsarević has achieved two victories over a World No. 1 player, having defeated compatriot Novak Djokovic twice.","title":"Janko Tipsarević"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" He also has thirteen victories against other players in the top 10: four wins against Tomáš Berdych, and one each against Fernando González, Mikhail Youzhny, David Ferrer, James Blake, Gaël Monfils, Andy Murray and Juan Mónaco.","title":"Janko Tipsarević"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" He holds victories over former World No. 1 players Carlos Moyá, Marat Safin, Lleyton Hewitt, Juan Carlos Ferrero and Andy Roddick.","title":"Janko Tipsarević"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" His best results at a Grand Slam have been reaching the quarterfinals at the US Open in 2011 and 2012.","title":"Janko Tipsarević"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":8,"text":" He is only the second Serb to reach the final 16 at all four different grand slams.","title":"Janko Tipsarević"}
