Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mark Fuhrman (born February 5, 1952) is a former detective of the Los Angeles Police Department (LAPD).","title":"Mark Fuhrman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is primarily known for his part in the investigation of the murders of Nicole Brown Simpson and Ron Goldman in the O.J. Simpson murder case.","title":"Mark Fuhrman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"After serving as publicity director of St. Martin’s Press, Grosset & Dunlap and Harry N. Abrams, Ms. Wesman founded Jane Wesman Public Relations, a firm specializing in book publicity campaigns, in 1980.","title":"Jane Wesman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" While at Grosset & Dunlap she was in charge of the campaign for \"RN: The Memoirs of Richard Nixon\".","title":"Jane Wesman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Since then she has orchestrated the campaigns for \"Murder in Brentwood\", Mark Fuhrman's book about the O.J. Simpson murder trial, as well as Whitley Streiber's \"Communion\".","title":"Jane Wesman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Wesman also handled the publicity campaigns for \"You're Fifty — Now What?","title":"Jane Wesman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Investing for the Second Half of Your Life\" by Charles Schwab, \"The 8th Habit\" (Stephen R. Covey’s follow-up to \"The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People\") and both \"Codependent No More\" and \"Beyond Codependency\" by Melody Beattie.","title":"Jane Wesman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Other authors she has worked with include Mary Higgins Clark, Michael Hammer, Paolo Coehlo, and Alan C. Fox.","title":"Jane Wesman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Reunion is an American drama series that aired on FOX in late 2005.","title":"Reunion (TV series)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The series was intended to chronicle 20 years in the lives of a group of six high school friends from Bedford, New York, with each episode following one year in the lives of the six, beginning with their high school graduation year 1986.","title":"Reunion (TV series)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Each episode also featured scenes in the present where Detective Marjorino (Mathew St. Patrick) is investigating the brutal murder of one of the group during the night of their 20-year class reunion in 2006.","title":"Reunion (TV series)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The identity of the murder victim was not revealed until the fifth episode, \"1990\".","title":"Reunion (TV series)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lifeblood is a children's novel by Tom Becker, first published in 2007.","title":"Lifeblood (novel)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is the sequel to \"Darkside\", and the second in a planned series of five.","title":"Lifeblood (novel)"}
