Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Fuhrman tapes are 13 hours of taped interviews given by Los Angeles police officer Mark Fuhrman to writer Laura McKinny between 1985 and 1994.","title":"Fuhrman tapes"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The tapes include many racist slurs and remarks made by Fuhrman, including uses of the word \"nigger,\" descriptions of police brutality perpetrated on black suspects, misogynist slurs and descriptions of the harassment and intimidation of female Los Angeles police officers by male officers.","title":"Fuhrman tapes"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Portions of the tapes were admitted into evidence during the O. J. Simpson murder case.","title":"Fuhrman tapes"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" In the tapes Fuhrman also made many references to the \"planting of evidence\" and implied that police brutality and evidence planting were common practice in the Los Angeles Police Department.","title":"Fuhrman tapes"}
