Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Pacific Mall is an Asian shopping centre in Markham, Ontario, Canada.","title":"Pacific Mall"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located on the northeast side of Steeles Avenue and Kennedy Road, right across the municipal border from the city of Toronto, on the site formerly occupied by Cullen Country Barns.","title":"Pacific Mall"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The two entrance roads of the mall are Redlea Avenue and Clayton Drive.","title":"Pacific Mall"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Pacific Mall is surrounded by an existing shopping plaza, including the Market Village, and together they encompass over 500 stores and are served by both indoor and outdoor parking areas with over 1,500 parking spaces combined.","title":"Pacific Mall"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" It has two floors and an underground level that leads to an underground parking lot.","title":"Pacific Mall"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Designed by Wallman Clewes Bergman Architects, their first proposal was modified by the aesthetic expectations of Markham Town Council (now City Council).","title":"Pacific Mall"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" Pacific Mall first opened its doors for business in 1997.","title":"Pacific Mall"}
