Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Warm Springs is an unincorporated community in Deer Lodge County, Montana, United States, operated by the state of Montana.","title":"Warm Springs, Montana"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is the site of Montana State Hospital, the only long term psychiatric hospital operated by the state of Montana.","title":"Warm Springs, Montana"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The hospital was founded by the Territorial Government of Montana in 1877.","title":"Warm Springs, Montana"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The \"warm springs\" are located on the hospital campus.","title":"Warm Springs, Montana"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Hot water seeps from a limestone cone that is about 40 feet high.","title":"Warm Springs, Montana"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The Native Americans called this the \"Lodge of the Whitetailed Deer\" giving the Deer Lodge Valley its name.","title":"Warm Springs, Montana"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" There are no community services other than a bar and convenience store on the frontage road and a post office (zip code 59756) on the hospital campus.","title":"Warm Springs, Montana"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" Brown trout fishing can be found in the Clark Fork River just east of Warm Springs and in the ponds on the Warm Springs Wildlife Management Area.","title":"Warm Springs, Montana"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Eastern Shore Hospital Center is an 76-bed psychiatric facility that is located in Cambridge, Maryland.","title":"Eastern Shore Hospital Center"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is owned and operated by the State of Maryland.","title":"Eastern Shore Hospital Center"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Levels of care provided include acute and long-term inpatient psychiatric hospital services for adults aged 18 and older.","title":"Eastern Shore Hospital Center"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The Center also operates an on-site 16-bed residential Assisted Living Program that is known as Stepping Stone at Manokin.","title":"Eastern Shore Hospital Center"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The 40-bed Upper Shore Community Mental Health Center, a psychiatric hospital that was located in Chestertown, and the Eastern Shore Hospital Center were jointly administered for a number of years.","title":"Eastern Shore Hospital Center"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The Upper Shore Community Mental Health Center was closed in March 2010.","title":"Eastern Shore Hospital Center"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"A hospital is a health care institution providing patient treatment with specialized medical and nursing staff and medical equipment.","title":"Hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The best-known type of hospital is the general hospital, which typically has an emergency department to treat urgent health problems ranging from fire and accident victims to a heart attack.","title":"Hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" A district hospital typically is the major health care facility in its region, with large numbers of beds for intensive care and additional beds for patients who need long-term care.","title":"Hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Specialised hospitals include trauma centres, rehabilitation hospitals, children's hospitals, seniors' (geriatric) hospitals, and hospitals for dealing with specific medical needs such as psychiatric treatment (see psychiatric hospital) and certain disease categories.","title":"Hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Specialised hospitals can help reduce health care costs compared to general hospitals.","title":"Hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"A state hospital is a hospital funded and operated by the government of a state.","title":"State hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" In some countries, such as South Africa, the term is synonymous with public hospital.","title":"State hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" In other countries, like the United States, general public hospitals are operated by local governments.","title":"State hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Due in part to the efforts of Dorothea Dix, the term \"state hospital\" generally refers to a public psychiatric hospital operated by a state government for persons committed to compulsory psychiatric care after being found not guilty of serious violent crimes on the basis of insanity.","title":"State hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Morningside Hospital was a psychiatric hospital in Portland, Oregon, United States.","title":"Morningside Hospital (Oregon)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" For nearly sixty years the hospital sat on a 47-acre parcel at the junction of SE Stark Street and 96th Avenue.","title":"Morningside Hospital (Oregon)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Formerly agricultural land, the site was developed as a psychiatric hospital complex and working farm in 1910.","title":"Morningside Hospital (Oregon)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" After World War II, many of the farmers in the surrounding area retired and their land was developed into suburban communities.","title":"Morningside Hospital (Oregon)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The rising population increased consumer demand and the under-construction interstate freeway promised easy access.","title":"Morningside Hospital (Oregon)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"St. Conal's Hospital (Irish: Ospidéal Naomh Conaill) is a psychiatric hospital located in Letterkenny, County Donegal, Ireland.","title":"St. Conal's Psychiatric Hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Situated adjacent to Letterkenny Town Park near Letterkenny University Hospital, it is the only psychiatric hospital located in County Donegal and is considered to be \"\"one of the finest buildings in the country\"\".","title":"St. Conal's Psychiatric Hospital"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) has been carried out on patients here.","title":"St. Conal's Psychiatric Hospital"}

