Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Boyle was presented with the Extraordinary Contribution to Filmmaking Award at the 2008 Austin Film Festival, where he also introduced that year's AFF Audience Award Winner \"Slumdog Millionaire\".","title":"Danny Boyle"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"William Oliver Stone (born September 15, 1946) is an American screenwriter, film producer, and director of motion pictures and documentaries.","title":"Oliver Stone"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Stone won an Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay as writer of \"Midnight Express\" (1978).","title":"Oliver Stone"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" He also wrote the acclaimed gangster movie \"Scarface\" (1983).","title":"Oliver Stone"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" As a director, Stone achieved prominence as director/writer of the war drama \"Platoon\" (1986), for which Stone won the Academy Award for Best Director; the film was awarded Best Picture.","title":"Oliver Stone"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" \"Platoon\" was the first in a trilogy of films based on the Vietnam War, in which Stone served as an infantry soldier.","title":"Oliver Stone"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" He continued the series with \"Born on the Fourth of July\" (1989)—for which Stone won his second Best Director Oscar—and \"Heaven & Earth\" (1993).","title":"Oliver Stone"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" Stone's other notable works include the Salvadoran Civil War-based drama \"Salvador\" (1986); the financial drama \"Wall Street\" (1987) and its 2010 sequel \"\"; the Jim Morrison biopic \"The Doors\" (1991); and a trilogy of films based on the American Presidency—\"JFK\" (1991), \"Nixon\" (1995) and \"W.\" (2008).","title":"Oliver Stone"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" His latest film is \"Snowden\" (2016).","title":"Oliver Stone"}
