Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Richard Stuart Linklater ( ; born July 30, 1960) is an American filmmaker, screenwriter, and actor.","title":"Richard Linklater"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Linklater is mostly known for his realistic and natural humanist films which mainly revolve around suburban culture and the effects of the passage of time.","title":"Richard Linklater"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Some notable films of his include the observational comedy film \"Slacker\" (1990), the coming-of-age comedy \"Dazed and Confused\" (1993), the romantic drama film trilogy \"Before Sunrise\" (1995), \"Before Sunset\" (2004), and \"Before Midnight\" (2013); the music-themed comedy \"School of Rock\" (2003), and the rotoscope animated \"Waking Life\" (2001) and \"A Scanner Darkly\" (2006).","title":"Richard Linklater"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" In 2002 he began filming \"Boyhood\" (2014), a passion project which took over twelve years to finish.","title":"Richard Linklater"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The film was premiered in 2014 to critical acclaim.","title":"Richard Linklater"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Linklater won the Golden Globe, Critics' Choice Movie Awards, and BAFTAs for Best Director and Best Picture.","title":"Richard Linklater"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" He also received his first nomination for the Academy Award for Best Director, along with nominations for Original Screenplay and Picture.","title":"Richard Linklater"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" In 2015, \"Time\" magazine named Linklater one of the 100 most influential people in the world on the annual \"Time 100\" list.","title":"Richard Linklater"}
