Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Napalm Beach is an American punk rock band from Portland, Oregon.","title":"Napalm Beach"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" One of the longest-running punk bands in the U.S., they are credited by some as being early innovators of the grunge sound.","title":"Napalm Beach"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Nicholas Pell, writing for the \"Portland Mercury\" said \"a huge influence on the grunge and alternative rock of the 1990s, Napalm Beach never had the name recognition of other Portland bands like Poison Idea or the Wipers.\"","title":"Napalm Beach"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Napalm Beach shared the stage with bands such as X, Public Image Ltd., Joan Jett, Johnny Thunders, Gun Club, Bad Brains, Soundgarden, Screaming Trees, Mudhoney, Dead Moon, and Poison Idea.","title":"Napalm Beach"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" They also toured Germany five times between 1989 and 1992.","title":"Napalm Beach"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" During their long musical career they have released more than 30 studio and live recordings in various formats on a number of small independent labels in the U.S. and Germany.","title":"Napalm Beach"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Van Conner (born March 17, 1967 in Apple Valley, California) is an American rock musician.","title":"Van Conner"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" In 1984 he co-founded the band Screaming Trees with his brother Gary Lee Conner and close friends Mark Lanegan and Mark Pickerel.","title":"Van Conner"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" On the 25 June 2000 Screaming Trees announced their official breakup.","title":"Van Conner"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Conner would start a low key band under the name Gardener which released its only album in the 1990s under the name \"New Dawning Time\".","title":"Van Conner"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Conner has also had brief appearances as a session musician with other known bands such as Queens of the Stone Age and helping Mark Lanegan on his solo album I'll Take Care of You.","title":"Van Conner"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Clairvoyance is the 1986 debut studio album by the alternative rock band Screaming Trees, produced by Steve Fisk.","title":"Clairvoyance (album)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Released on Velvetone Records, the album helped the band earn a contract with SST Records.","title":"Clairvoyance (album)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" While it is very much a combination of psychedelic and garage rock, it bears many similarities to early grunge.","title":"Clairvoyance (album)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"\"Nearly Lost You\" is a song by the American alternative rock group Screaming Trees.","title":"Nearly Lost You"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is the first single released in support of their sixth album \"Sweet Oblivion\".","title":"Nearly Lost You"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Perhaps their best-known song, it was a moderate success on modern rock radio, partly because of its appearance on the to the 1992 Cameron Crowe film \"Singles\".","title":"Nearly Lost You"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" In addition to the soundtrack, \"Nearly Lost You\" also appeared on the band's 1992 breakthrough album \"Sweet Oblivion\".","title":"Nearly Lost You"}
