Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" It expresses the faith and aspiration of seeing that person again on \"the other side\".","title":"The Other Side (Paul van Dyk song)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"\"For An Angel\" is a trance debut track by German DJ Paul van Dyk.","title":"For an Angel"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" His most famous track, it was initially released in 1994 as a track on \"45 RPM\" on the MFS record label, which was van Dyk's first studio album.","title":"For an Angel"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was later reworked and re-released in 1998 as \"E-Werk Remix\" on Deviant Records, a homage to the E-Werk nightclub where van Dyk used to be the resident DJ, the song reached number-one on the UK Dance Chart for several weeks.","title":"For an Angel"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Since its release the track has become one of the most influential and greatest trance tracks of all time.","title":"For an Angel"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" It was voted by \"Mixmag\" readers as the eighth greatest dance record of all time.","title":"For an Angel"}

