Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" He was drafted 21st overall in the 2016 NBA draft by the Atlanta Hawks.","title":"DeAndre' Bembry"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 2007–08 NBA season was the Atlanta Hawks' 59th season in the National Basketball Association, and 40th season in Atlanta.","title":"2007–08 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" After missing the playoffs for eight straight seasons, the Hawks selected Al Horford out of the University of Florida with the third pick in the 2007 NBA draft.","title":"2007–08 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Hawks started out the season by defeating the Dallas Mavericks 101–94 in their season opener, marking the first time they won their first game of the season since the 1999 lockout season.","title":"2007–08 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" However, their struggles continued as they went on a six-game losing streak around the All-Star break.","title":"2007–08 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" At midseason, the Hawks traded Tyronn Lue, Lorenzen Wright, Anthony Johnson and second-year forward Shelden Williams to the Sacramento Kings for Mike Bibby.","title":"2007–08 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The Hawks finished third in the Southeast Division with a 37–45 record, and made the playoffs for the first time since 1999.","title":"2007–08 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" Joe Johnson was selected for the 2008 NBA All-Star Game, and Horford made the All-First Rookie Team.","title":"2007–08 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" In the first round of the playoffs, they lost to the top-seeded Boston Celtics in seven games.","title":"2007–08 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":8,"text":" Following the season, Josh Childress left to play overseas.","title":"2007–08 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Hawks entered the season with rookies Jon Koncak and Spud Webb.","title":"1985–86 Atlanta Hawks season"}
