Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Hawks were led by \"the Human Highlight Reel\" Dominique Wilkins.","title":"1985–86 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" He would have an outstanding year as he led the NBA in scoring with an average of 30.3 points per game.","title":"1985–86 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" One of the highlights of the season came when Webb (measuring five feet, seven inches) won the NBA Slam Dunk contest during All-Star Weekend.","title":"1985–86 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" In the second half of the season, the Hawks would be one of the strongest teams in the league.","title":"1985–86 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" The club won 35 of their final 52 games to finish the season with a record of 50 wins and 32 losses.","title":"1985–86 Atlanta Hawks season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" In the playoffs, the Hawks would eliminate the Detroit Pistons in 4 games.","title":"1985–86 Atlanta Hawks season"}
