Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" As co-inventor and co-founding CEO, Fisher built three companies including Bharosa—which produced the Oracle Adaptive Access Manager and sold to Oracle Corporation for a reported $50 million in 2007, NetClerk—now part of Roper Technologies and AutoReach—now part of AutoNation.","title":"Jon Fisher"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Carnegie Mellon Silicon Valley is a branch campus of Carnegie Mellon University located in the heart of Silicon Valley in Mountain View, California.","title":"Carnegie Mellon Silicon Valley"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was established in 2002 at the NASA Ames Research Center in Moffett Field.","title":"Carnegie Mellon Silicon Valley"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The campus offers full-time and part-time professional Masters programs in Electrical And Computer Engineering, Software Engineering and Software Management, various bi-coastal (split-time between Pittsburgh and Silicon Valley) Masters programs in Information Technology, and a bi-coastal Ph.D. program in Electrical and Computer Engineering.","title":"Carnegie Mellon Silicon Valley"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" One key differentiator between programs in the traditional Pittsburgh campus and the new Silicon Valley campus is a new focus on project-centered \"learning by doing\" approach to education.","title":"Carnegie Mellon Silicon Valley"}

