Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"\"Hot Rod Lincoln\" is a song by American singer-songwriter Charlie Ryan, first released in 1955.","title":"Hot Rod Lincoln"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was written as an answer song to Arkie Shibley's 1951 hit \"Hot Rod Race\" which describes a race in San Pedro, Los Angeles between two hot rod cars, a Ford and a Mercury, which stay neck-and-neck until both are overtaken by \"a kid in a hopped-up Model A\".","title":"Hot Rod Lincoln"}
