Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Gmelina leichhardtii, commonly known as the white beech is a rainforest tree of eastern Australia.","title":"Gmelina leichhardtii"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Scattered individuals or small groups of trees naturally occur from the Illawarra district of New South Wales (34½° S) to near Proserpine in tropical Queensland.","title":"Gmelina leichhardtii"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The white beech or grey teak is a fast-growing tree, growing on volcanic and alluvial soils in areas of moderate to high rainfall.","title":"Gmelina leichhardtii"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" It also grows on poorer sedimentary soils in fire free areas.","title":"Gmelina leichhardtii"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" White beech may occasionally be seen in Australian rainforests, their status is considered \"uncommon\".","title":"Gmelina leichhardtii"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Unlike the Australian red cedar, the white beech has not recovered particularly well after logging in the 19th and 20th centuries.","title":"Gmelina leichhardtii"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Pinus strobiformis, commonly known as Southwestern white pine, Mexican white pine or Chihuahua white pine, is a medium-sized white pine tree whose native habitat is in southwestern United States and Mexico.","title":"Pinus strobiformis"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is typically a high-elevation pine growing mixed with other conifers (a Montane forest).","title":"Pinus strobiformis"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Idumuje Unor is a town situated in the Aniocha North Local Government Area of Delta State, Nigeria, lying between 6020’ 01.4’’ N and 60 22’ 06.5’’ N and between 60 25’ 01.4’’ E and 60 27’ 06.6’’ E.","title":"Idumuje-Unor"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located 5 kilometers from Issele-Uku, the headquarters of Aniocha North and has a growing land area of 16sq km and current estimated population of about 10,000 inhabitants.","title":"Idumuje-Unor"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is bordered to the west by Onicha-Ugbo, to the North by Idumuje-Ugboko and Ewohinmi in Edo State, to the East by Onicha-Uku and to the south by Issele-Uku.","title":"Idumuje-Unor"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The name Idumuje in the Esan language could be translated to mean; Idumu - Community/Quarters and Oje - King/Royal.","title":"Idumuje-Unor"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" In other words, Idumuje means Royal Quarters or Kings' Quarter.","title":"Idumuje-Unor"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Worthy to note: Another Idumuje named location could be found at present in Benin (in proximity to the Royal Palace of the Oba of Benin).","title":"Idumuje-Unor"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" The suffix \"Unor\" (meaning - home) is an inclusion to the town's name so as to differentiate it from the breakaway community Idumuje -Ugboko; by a man called Nwoko and his supporters some 300 years ago.","title":"Idumuje-Unor"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" Ugboko is translated to mean \"Ugbo\" - Farm & \"Oko\" - a shortening of the name Nwoko.","title":"Idumuje-Unor"}
