Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The polar bear (\"Ursus maritimus\") is a carnivorous bear whose native range lies largely within the Arctic Circle, encompassing the Arctic Ocean, its surrounding seas and surrounding land masses.","title":"Polar bear"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a large bear, approximately the same size as the omnivorous Kodiak bear (\"Ursus arctos middendorffi\").","title":"Polar bear"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" A boar (adult male) weighs around 350 – , while a sow (adult female) is about half that size.","title":"Polar bear"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Although it is the sister species of the brown bear, it has evolved to occupy a narrower ecological niche, with many body characteristics adapted for cold temperatures, for moving across snow, ice and open water, and for hunting seals, which make up most of its diet.","title":"Polar bear"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Although most polar bears are born on land, they spend most of their time on the sea ice.","title":"Polar bear"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Their scientific name means \"maritime bear\" and derives from this fact.","title":"Polar bear"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" Polar bears hunt their preferred food of seals from the edge of sea ice, often living off fat reserves when no sea ice is present.","title":"Polar bear"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" Because of their dependence on the sea ice, polar bears are classified as marine mammals.","title":"Polar bear"}
