Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" She was narrowly defeated by incumbent Representative Mike Ferguson in 2006 but lost by a wider margin to Leonard Lance in the November 4, 2008 election.","title":"Linda Stender"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The New Jersey Folk Festival is an annual folk music and cultural festival held on the Great Lawn of the Eagleton Institute of Politics on the Douglass Campus at Rutgers University in New Brunswick, New Jersey.","title":"New Jersey Folk Festival"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a free, non-profit family event held every year on the last Saturday in April from 10am - 6pm, rain or shine.","title":"New Jersey Folk Festival"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" It coincides with Rutgers Agricultural Field Day held on the adjacent Cook Campus.","title":"New Jersey Folk Festival"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Beginning in 2009, both the New Jersey Folk Festival and Ag Field Day are held as a major part of Rutgers Day.","title":"New Jersey Folk Festival"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Leonard Cooke (born April 29, 1982) is an American former high school and professional basketball player.","title":"Lenny Cooke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Born in Atlantic City, New Jersey, he is known primarily for having been ranked higher than LeBron James and Carmelo Anthony in the Summer of 2001.","title":"Lenny Cooke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" He had averaged 25 points, 10 rebounds, two steals, and two blocks per game in his junior year of high school.","title":"Lenny Cooke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Following his junior year in high school, he averaged 31.5 points for the first eight games of his senior year.","title":"Lenny Cooke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" When he turned 19 in 2001, he was academically ineligible to play according to high school athletics' rules in his home county in New Jersey.","title":"Lenny Cooke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Cooke is the subject of the 2013 Tribeca Film Festival selected documentary film \"Lenny Cooke\" by the Safdie Brothers.","title":"Lenny Cooke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Leonard J. Lance (born June 25, 1952) is the U.S. Representative for New Jersey 's 7 congressional district , serving since 2009.","title":"Leonard Lance"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is a member of the Republican Party.","title":"Leonard Lance"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" He previously served in the New Jersey Senate and the New Jersey General Assembly where he had been lauded by legislative peers as a moderate Republican.","title":"Leonard Lance"}
