Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Heckscher State Parkway (formerly known as the Heckscher Spur) is an 8.24 mi parkway on Long Island, New York, in the United States.","title":"Heckscher State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The parkway, located entirely within the Suffolk County town of Islip, begins at the south end of the Sagtikos State Parkway in West Islip, from where it continues west as the Southern State Parkway.","title":"Heckscher State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" It proceeds east as a six-lane parkway through Brentwood and Central Islip, loosely paralleling New York State Route 27 (NY 27).","title":"Heckscher State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" At Islip Terrace, the Heckscher Parkway turns southward, crossing NY 27 before ending at the toll barrier for Heckscher State Park in Great River.","title":"Heckscher State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The parkway comprises the eastern portion of New York State Route 908M (NY 908M), an unsigned reference route, with the Southern State Parkway occupying the western section.","title":"Heckscher State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" In order to avoid confusion, the highway is signed as an extension of the Southern State Parkway west of the NY 27 interchange (exit 44).","title":"Heckscher State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Garden State Parkway (GSP) is a 172.4 mi limited-access toll parkway that stretches the length of New Jersey from the New York line at Montvale to Cape May at the state's southernmost tip.","title":"Garden State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Its name refers to New Jersey's nickname, the \"Garden State\".","title":"Garden State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Most New Jerseyans refer to it as simply \"the Parkway\".","title":"Garden State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The parkway's official, but unsigned, designation is Route 444.","title":"Garden State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" At its north end, the parkway becomes the Garden State Parkway Connector, a component of the New York State Thruway system that connects to the Thruway mainline in Ramapo.","title":"Garden State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The Parkway is primarily for passenger vehicle use, with trucks weighing over 10,000 pounds prohibited north of Exit 105.","title":"Garden State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" The Parkway has been ranked as the busiest toll highway in the country based on the number of toll transactions.","title":"Garden State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" At roughly 172 miles, the Parkway is the longest highway in the state.","title":"Garden State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Meadowbrook State Parkway (also known as the Meadowbrook, the Meadowbrook Parkway or the MSP) is a 12.52 mi parkway in Nassau County, New York, in the United States.","title":"Meadowbrook State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Its southern terminus is at a full cloverleaf interchange with the Bay and Ocean parkways in Jones Beach State Park.","title":"Meadowbrook State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The parkway heads north, crossing South Oyster Bay and intersecting Loop Parkway before crossing onto the mainland and connecting to the Southern State Parkway in North Merrick.","title":"Meadowbrook State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" It continues north to the village of Carle Place, where the Meadowbrook Parkway ends at exit 31A of the Northern State Parkway.","title":"Meadowbrook State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The Meadowbrook Parkway is designated New York State Route 908E (NY 908E), an unsigned reference route.","title":"Meadowbrook State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Most of the road is limited to non-commercial traffic, like most parkways in the state of New York; however, the portion south of Merrick Road is open to commercial traffic.","title":"Meadowbrook State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Great Egg Harbor Bridge is a toll bridge along the Garden State Parkway in New Jersey, with tolls collected in the southbound direction.","title":"Great Egg Harbor Bridge"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It crosses the Great Egg Harbor Bay, connecting Upper Township, in Cape May County to Somers Point in Atlantic County.","title":"Great Egg Harbor Bridge"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The bridge crosses over a section of Egg Harbor Township.","title":"Great Egg Harbor Bridge"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" It carries a portion of the Garden State Parkway and U.S. Route 9.","title":"Great Egg Harbor Bridge"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Sunken Meadow State Parkway (also known as the Sunken Meadow) is a 6.19 mi long parkway in Suffolk County, Long Island, New York.","title":"Sunken Meadow State Parkway"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Located entirely within the town of Smithtown, the parkway begins at a cloverleaf interchange with the Northern State Parkway (exits 44–45) and the northern terminus of the Sagtikos State Parkway.","title":"Sunken Meadow State Parkway"}
