Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Clement Richard Attlee, 1st Earl Attlee, {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (3 January 1883 – 8 October 1967) was a British Labour politician who served as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 1945 to 1951 and Leader of the Labour Party from 1935 to 1955.","title":"Clement Attlee"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" In 1940, Attlee took Labour into the wartime coalition government and served under Winston Churchill, becoming the first person to hold the office of Deputy Prime Minister of the United Kingdom.","title":"Clement Attlee"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" He went on to lead the Labour Party to an unexpected landslide victory at the 1945 general election; forming the first Labour majority government, and a mandate to implement its postwar reforms.","title":"Clement Attlee"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The 12.0% national swing from the Conservatives to Labour was unprecedented at that time and remains the largest ever achieved by any party at a general election in British electoral history.","title":"Clement Attlee"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" He was re-elected with a narrow majority at the 1950 general election.","title":"Clement Attlee"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" In the following year, Attlee called a snap general election, hoping to increase his parliamentary majority.","title":"Clement Attlee"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" However, he was narrowly defeated by the Conservatives under the leadership of Winston Churchill; despite winning the most votes of any political party in any general election in British political history until the Conservative Party's fourth consecutive victory in 1992.","title":"Clement Attlee"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" Attlee remains the longest-ever serving Leader of the Labour Party.","title":"Clement Attlee"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Conservative Party, officially the Conservative and Unionist Party, is a centre-right political party in the United Kingdom.","title":"Conservative Party (UK)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is currently the governing party, having been so since the 2010 general election, where a coalition government with the Liberal Democrats was formed.","title":"Conservative Party (UK)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 2015, the Conservatives led by David Cameron won a surprise majority and formed the first Conservative majority government since 1992.","title":"Conservative Party (UK)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" However, the 2017 snap election on Thursday 8 June resulted in a hung parliament, and the Conservatives lost their parliamentary majority.","title":"Conservative Party (UK)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" They are reliant on the support of a Northern Irish political party, the Democratic Unionist Party (DUP), in order to command a majority in the House of Commons through a confidence-and-supply deal.","title":"Conservative Party (UK)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The party leader, Theresa May, has served as both Leader of the Conservative Party and Prime Minister since 13 July 2016.","title":"Conservative Party (UK)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" It is the largest party in local government with 9,237 councillors.","title":"Conservative Party (UK)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" The Conservative Party is one of the two major contemporary political parties in the United Kingdom, the other being its modern rival, the Labour Party.","title":"Conservative Party (UK)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":8,"text":" The Conservative Party's platform involves support for free market capitalism, free enterprise, fiscal conservatism, a strong national defence, deregulation, and restrictions on trade unions.","title":"Conservative Party (UK)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 1997 Conservative Party leadership election was triggered in the British Conservative Party when John Major resigned on 2 May 1997, following his party's defeat at the 1997 general election, which ended 18 years of Conservative Government of the United Kingdom.","title":"Conservative Party (UK) leadership election, 1997"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Major had been Conservative leader and Prime Minister since November 1990.","title":"Conservative Party (UK) leadership election, 1997"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Federation of Conservative Students (FCS) was the student organisation of the British Conservative Party from the late 1940s to 1986.","title":"Federation of Conservative Students"}
