Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Regional Planning Association of America (\"RPAA\"), formed by Clarence Stein was an urban reform association developed in 1923.","title":"Regional Planning Association of America"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The association was a diverse group of people all with their own talents and skills.","title":"Regional Planning Association of America"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The goal of this group was to “connect a diverse group of friends in a critical examination of the city, in the collaborative development and dissemination of ideas, in political action and in city building projects”.","title":"Regional Planning Association of America"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Throughout the ten-year span in which the association lasted, five leading members contributed to this goal.","title":"Regional Planning Association of America"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Clarence Stein, Benton MacKaye, Lewis Mumford, Alexander Bing, and Henry Wright were the essential backbone of the RPAA.","title":"Regional Planning Association of America"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Originally an idea of Clarence Stein’s, through a series of introductions and acquaintances in Washington DC in 1918, the Regional Planning Association began to form.","title":"Regional Planning Association of America"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lewis Mumford, KBE (October 19, 1895 – January 26, 1990) was an American historian, sociologist, philosopher of technology, and literary critic.","title":"Lewis Mumford"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Particularly noted for his study of cities and urban architecture, he had a broad career as a writer.","title":"Lewis Mumford"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Mumford was influenced by the work of Scottish theorist Sir Patrick Geddes and worked closely with his associate the British sociologist Victor Branford.","title":"Lewis Mumford"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Technics and Civilization is a 1934 book by American philosopher and historian of technology Lewis Mumford.","title":"Technics and Civilization"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The book presents the history of technology and its role in shaping and being shaped by civilizations.","title":"Technics and Civilization"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" According to Mumford, modern technology has its roots in the Middle Ages rather than in the Industrial Revolution.","title":"Technics and Civilization"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" It is the moral, economic, and political choices we make, not the machines we use, Mumford argues, that have produced a capitalist industrialized machine-oriented economy, whose imperfect fruits serve the majority so imperfectly.","title":"Technics and Civilization"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Thom Nickels is a conservative commentator and Philadelphia-based author of nine literary works and previous recipient of the 2005 Philadelphia AIA Lewis Mumford Architecture Journalism Award, and was nominated for a Lambda Literary Award and a Hugo Award for his book, Two Novellas.","title":"Thom Nickels"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The City in History: Its Origins, Its Transformations, and Its Prospects is a 1961 National Book Award winner by American historian Lewis Mumford.","title":"The City in History"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Myth of the Machine is a two-volume book taking an in-depth look at the forces that have shaped modern technology since prehistoric times.","title":"The Myth of the Machine"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The first volume, \"Technics and Human Development\", was published in 1967, followed by the second volume, \"The Pentagon of Power\", in 1970.","title":"The Myth of the Machine"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The author, Lewis Mumford, shows the parallel developments between human tools and social organization mainly through language and rituals.","title":"The Myth of the Machine"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" It is considered a synthesis of many theories Mumford developed throughout his prolific writing career.","title":"The Myth of the Machine"}
