Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Inauguration of Millard Fillmore, as the 13th President of the United States, was held on Wednesday, July 10, 1850 at the United States Capitol in Washington, D.C., following the death of President Zachary Taylor the previous day.","title":"Inauguration of Millard Fillmore"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" President Zachary Taylor died from a severe intestinal illness which subsequently thrust Millard Fillmore into the role of President .","title":"Inauguration of Millard Fillmore"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The inauguration marked the commencement of Millard Fillmore's only term (a partial term of ) as President, but he faced a stressful climate .","title":"Inauguration of Millard Fillmore"}
