Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Popular activities at the convention included filking (filk singing is a play on folk) and gaming.","title":"Conestoga (convention)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Featured programming included a writers track, an art show, a dealer room, a masquerade, and a play put on by the Penguin Playhouse Troupe.","title":"Conestoga (convention)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Dungeness School is a historical schoolhouse building located at 657 Towne Road in Dungeness, Washington.","title":"Dungeness School"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The idea for the school was formed in 1892 by the settlers of the Dungeness area.","title":"Dungeness School"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" On May 10, 1892 a meeting was held in which settlers created a bond for land and a two story school house.","title":"Dungeness School"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The school house opened on February 27, 1893.","title":"Dungeness School"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The school originally had 73 students from the ages of 5 to 20.","title":"Dungeness School"}
