Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Edward Michael \"Mike\"/\"Spanky\" Fincke (born March 14, 1967) is an American astronaut who formerly held the American record for the most time in space (381.6 days).","title":"Michael Fincke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" His record was broken by Scott Kelly on October 16, 2015.","title":"Michael Fincke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" He was born in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, but considers its suburb Emsworth to be his hometown.","title":"Michael Fincke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" He is a United States Air Force officer and a NASA astronaut, and served two tours aboard the International Space Station as a flight engineer and commander.","title":"Michael Fincke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" He flew on one Space Shuttle mission, STS-134 as a Mission Specialist.","title":"Michael Fincke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Fincke is conversant in Japanese and Russian.","title":"Michael Fincke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" He is married to Renita Saikia, and together they have three children; son Chandra and daughters Tarali and Surya.","title":"Michael Fincke"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Scott Joseph Kelly (born February 21, 1964 in Orange, New Jersey) is an engineer, retired American astronaut, and a retired U.S. Navy Captain.","title":"Scott Kelly (astronaut)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" A veteran of four space flights, Kelly commanded the International Space Station (ISS) on Expeditions 26, 45, and 46.","title":"Scott Kelly (astronaut)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The One-Year Mission on the International Space Station is a scientific research project that studies the health effects of long term spaceflight.","title":"ISS year long mission"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Scott Kelly and Mikhail Korniyenko spent 342 days in space, with scientists performing medical experiments.","title":"ISS year long mission"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Kelly and Kornienko launched on 27 March 2015 on Soyuz TMA-16M along with Gennady Padalka.","title":"ISS year long mission"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The mission encompassed Expeditions 43, 44, 45 and 46.","title":"ISS year long mission"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The pair safely landed in Kazakhstan on March 2, 2016, returning aboard Soyuz TMA-18M with Sergey Volkov.","title":"ISS year long mission"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The mission supported the NASA Twins study, which helps shed light on the health effects of long duration spaceflight, which is of interest for Mars missions especially.","title":"ISS year long mission"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Expedition 45 was the 45th expedition to the International Space Station.","title":"Expedition 45"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Scott Kelly and Mikhail Korniyenko transferred from Expedition 44 as part of their year-long stay aboard the ISS.","title":"Expedition 45"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Expedition 45 began with the arrival of Soyuz TMA-18M at the ISS on September 11, 2015, and concluded with the departure of Soyuz TMA-17M on December 11 2015.","title":"Expedition 45"}
