Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Handheld camera, shaky cam, queasy cam, queasicam, hand-held camera or free camera is a cinematographic technique where stable-image techniques are purposely dispensed with.","title":"Shaky camera"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The camera is held in the hand, or given the appearance of being hand-held, and in many cases shots are limited to what one photographer could have accomplished with one camera.","title":"Shaky camera"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Shaky cam is often employed to give a film sequence an ad hoc, electronic news-gathering, or documentary film feel.","title":"Shaky camera"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" It suggests unprepared, unrehearsed filming of reality, and can provide a sense of dynamics, immersion, instability or nervousness.","title":"Shaky camera"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The technique can be used to give a pseudo-documentary or \"cinéma vérité\" appearance to a film.","title":"Shaky camera"}
