Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" He was invited to run as a Green Party candidate in September 2008.","title":"Martin Balluch"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ady Gil is an Israeli animal rights activist living in Hollywood, California, United States of America.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is a vegan.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Gil was raised in Ramat Gan, he joined the Israel Air Force from where he retired at the age of 22.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" He emigrated to USA.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" There in partnership with Erez Ram, also a veteran of the Israeli Defence Forces, he founded in 1992, American Hi Definition Inc, a company involved in high definition big screen video projection.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" In 1997 with Erez Ram and Joe Shckelford they started another company , Sweetwater Digital.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" In November 2010, the companies were acquired by NEP Broadcasting.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" After this sale Gil became a full time animal rights activist.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":8,"text":" He donated USD 6 million to his organization Ady Gil World Conservation.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":9,"text":" Gil set up a shelter for cats and dogs in Los Angeles and paid for sterilization of 6000 cats in Israel.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":10,"text":" He built a large roosting structure for eagles in a wildlife sanctuary on Mount Carmel.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":11,"text":" Gil donated millions to Sea Shepherd Conservation Society to refurbish a ship for use for its anti-whaling campaigns, the ship was given his name Ady Gil, the ship suffered sinking 290 km from Antarctica as a result of an incident with the Japanese ship Shonan Maru No 2 used for killing whales.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":12,"text":" The loss of the ship has been the subject of litigation between Gil and Paul Watson founder and director of Sea Shepherd Conservation Society.","title":"Ady Gil"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":13,"text":" In December 2014, Gil paid USD 2 million to rescue 1300 monkeys from a facility that bred them so that they would not be exported to the United States for being subjected to experiments that maimed and killed them.","title":"Ady Gil"}

