Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Umbilical cord prolapse occurs when the umbilical cord comes out of the uterus with or before the presenting part of the fetus.","title":"Umbilical cord prolapse"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a relatively rare condition and occurs in fewer than 1% of pregnancies.","title":"Umbilical cord prolapse"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Cord prolapse is more common in women who have had rupture of their amniotic sac.","title":"Umbilical cord prolapse"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Other risk factors include maternal or fetal factors that prevent the fetus from occupying a normal position in the maternal pelvis, such as abnormal fetal lie, too much amniotic fluid, or a premature or small fetus.","title":"Umbilical cord prolapse"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The concern with cord prolapse is that pressure on the cord from the fetus will cause cord compression that compromises blood flow to the fetus.","title":"Umbilical cord prolapse"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Whenever there is a sudden decrease in fetal heart rate or abnormal fetal heart tracing, umbilical cord prolapse should be considered.","title":"Umbilical cord prolapse"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" Due to the possibility for fetal death and other complications, umbilical cord prolapse is considered an obstetric emergency during pregnancy or labor.","title":"Umbilical cord prolapse"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" Current management guidelines focus on quick delivery, which usually entails a cesarean section.","title":"Umbilical cord prolapse"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":8,"text":" With appropriate management, the majority of cases have good neonatal outcomes.","title":"Umbilical cord prolapse"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Dying Fetus are an American death metal band originally from Upper Marlboro, Maryland.","title":"Dying Fetus"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Formed in 1991, the group is known for their consistently hook-laden song structures, characterized by blast beats, complex riffing, slam riffs and heavy breakdowns. Additionally, their reality-based lyrics characterized by political/modern themes are notable in death metal.","title":"Dying Fetus"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Various line-up changes throughout the years have left John Gallagher the remaining original member, as well as the band's driving force.","title":"Dying Fetus"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" According to Gallagher, the band name was chosen while the members were of adolescent ages and was intended to be offensive.","title":"Dying Fetus"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" To date, Dying Fetus has released eight studio albums.","title":"Dying Fetus"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Weltmacht (German for \"World Power\") was an American black metal band formed in DeKalb, Illinois in 1998.","title":"Weltmacht"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Members of the band all went by pseudonyms: \"Lord Imperial\" (Neill Jameson), \"Akhenaten\" (Andrew Harris) and \"Cryptic Winter\" (Duane Timlin).","title":"Weltmacht"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" During this period, they also performed and/or recorded with Krieg (Lord Imperial's main outfit).","title":"Weltmacht"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Lyrical themes reveal a fascination with nihilism and war, rather than more common black metal themes such as Satanism, anti-Christian blasphemy and paganism.","title":"Weltmacht"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" After the demise of Weltmacht in 2002, Lord Imperial went on to form N.I.L. and Duane Timlin eventually joined Dying Fetus.","title":"Weltmacht"}
