Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" They qualified for the playoffs as a wild-card team as the #5 seed, and beat the #4 seed Tampa Bay Buccaneers (9–7), the top-seeded Dallas Cowboys (13–3), and the #2 seed Green Bay Packers (13–3) to become the National Football Conference representative in Super Bowl XLII.","title":"2007 New York Giants season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" There, they defeated the heavily favored and previously undefeated 18–0 New England Patriots and spoiled their perfect season.","title":"2007 New York Giants season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The 2007 New York Giants became the 9th wild card team in NFL history to reach the Super Bowl and the 5th wild card team to win the Super Bowl, and the very first NFC wild card to accomplish the feat.","title":"2007 New York Giants season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" They were the third team in history to win three road playoff games en route to a Super Bowl and set a league record for most consecutive road wins in a single season (11), though the Super Bowl is played on a neutral field rather than an opponent's stadium.","title":"2007 New York Giants season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" It was the 7th league championship season for the New York Giants and their first since they won Super Bowl XXV in 1991.","title":"2007 New York Giants season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 2010 Green Bay Packers season was the 91st season in the National Football League for the Packers and the 92nd season for the team overall.","title":"2010 Green Bay Packers season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Although they finished with only a respectable 10–6 record, good for a second-place finish in the NFC North, the Packers never lost a game by more than four points, and never trailed by more than seven the entire season, becoming the only team since the AFL-NFL merger in 1970 to accomplish this.","title":"2010 Green Bay Packers season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" All six of their regular season losses were by a combined 20 points.","title":"2010 Green Bay Packers season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" They entered the playoffs as the NFC's sixth seed.","title":"2010 Green Bay Packers season"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" After defeating the Philadelphia Eagles 21–16 in the Wild Card round, the Atlanta Falcons 48–21 in the Divisional round and the Chicago Bears 21–14 in the NFC Championship, the team advanced to Super Bowl XLV in which they faced the AFC's 2nd seed Pittsburgh Steelers.","title":"2010 Green Bay Packers season"}
