Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Jacob D. Robida (June 13, 1987 – February 5, 2006) was a Massachusetts teenager who attacked three patrons at a New Bedford gay bar on February 2, 2006.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He fled the state and drove to Charleston, West Virginia, where he kidnapped Jennifer Rena Dunlap Bailey and drove southwest.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" He was stopped by Gassville, Arkansas Police Officer James W. Sell at the Brass Door Restaurant parking lot on the afternoon of February 4, 2006 for an apparent traffic violation.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Robida shot and killed Sell and fled east.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" He turned onto Arkansas Highway 201 headed south and continued to Arkana, where he fired at Arkansas State Police Sgt. Van Nowlin.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Deputies from the Baxter County Sheriff's Office had a spike strip deployed a short distance away.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" Robida drove over the spike strip, flattening both front tires on his Pontiac.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" He continued to Arkansas Highway 5, where he turned south and drove into the small town of Norfork.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":8,"text":" In the middle of town he lost control of the car due to the front tires, spun out, and hit two parked vehicles.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":9,"text":" He then shot Bailey, his kidnap victim, in the head with a Ruger 9mm semi-automatic pistol, killing her instantly.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":10,"text":" Police then opened fire on Robida.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":11,"text":" He shot himself in the right side of the head.","title":"Jacob D. Robida"}
