Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"\"You Open My Eyes\" is a single by iconic Australian rock group Hoodoo Gurus which reached #43 on the ARIA Singles Charts.","title":"You Open My Eyes"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was released on BMG in February, 1994; and was written by Brad Shepherd.","title":"You Open My Eyes"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" This was the first Hoodoo Gurus single that was not written or co-written by Dave Faulkner.","title":"You Open My Eyes"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The B side, \"Something I Forgot to Say\", was written by Faulkner.","title":"You Open My Eyes"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The second B side was a cover of The Victims' \"Television Addict\" written by James Baker and Faulkner (both were members of The Victims and of Hoodoo Gurus).","title":"You Open My Eyes"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The music video for \"You Open My Eyes\" was directed by former Guru, Kimble Rendall and was their most expensive to date.","title":"You Open My Eyes"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Australian rock group Hoodoo Gurus have released nine studio albums, thirty-six singles, two extended plays, six compilation albums and four video albums. Formed in January 1981, the band was originally known as Le Hoodoo Gurus for the release of their first single, \"Leilani\", in October 1982.","title":"Hoodoo Gurus discography"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" As Hoodoo Gurus, the band signed with Big Time Records and premiered their debut album, \"Stoneage Romeos\", in March 1984.","title":"Hoodoo Gurus discography"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Also issued in the United States through A&M Records, the record remained atop the Alternative/College Albums Chart for four consecutive weeks, with it also becoming one of the most played albums of that year on the college network.","title":"Hoodoo Gurus discography"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The group's subsequent albums, \"Mars Needs Guitars!","title":"Hoodoo Gurus discography"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":"\", \"Blow Your Cool!","title":"Hoodoo Gurus discography"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":"\" and \"Magnum Cum Louder\", all reached the \"Billboard\" 200.","title":"Hoodoo Gurus discography"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"James Lawrence Baker (born 7 March 1954) is a rock musician from Perth, Western Australia.","title":"James Baker (musician)"}
