Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Dubrovniks were an Australian rock band which formed in August 1986 as The Adorable Ones.","title":"Dubrovniks"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Early in 1987 they changed their name, which acknowledges two of their founders, Roddy Radalj and Boris Sujdovic, birthplace in Dubrovnik, a town in Croatia.","title":"Dubrovniks"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Both Radalj and fellow founder James Baker had also founded Hoodoo Gurus (as Le Hoodoo Gurus) in 1981.","title":"Dubrovniks"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" All three had earlier associations in the Perth punk scene of the late 1970s.","title":"Dubrovniks"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The group issued four albums, \"Dubrovnik Blues\" (August 1989), \"Audio Sonic Love Affair\" (September 1990), \"Chrome\" (June 1992), and \"Medicine Wheel\" (1994), before disbanding in 1995.","title":"Dubrovniks"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Richard Grossman (born 28 November 1959) is an Australian rock musician who has played bass guitar for two iconic bands: Divinyls and Hoodoo Gurus.","title":"Richard Grossman (bassist)"}
