Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lawrence E. Lockman is an American lumber worker, lobbyist and political activist from Amherst, Maine, who has served as a Republican member of the Maine House of Representatives since 2012.","title":"Lawrence Lockman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" A 2014 article in \"Bangor Daily News\" documenting controversial statements he has made over the years on the subjects of rape, HIV, and homosexuality, has drawn attention from political websites such as \"Daily Kos\" and \"Salon.com\".","title":"Lawrence Lockman"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ralph W. 'Bud' Leavitt Jr. (1917–1994) was a Maine newspaperman who was executive sports editor of \"The Bangor Daily News\", and a longtime outdoor columnist recognized statewide.","title":"Ralph W. 'Bud' Leavitt Jr."}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" In addition to his writing, Leavitt hosted one of Maine's earliest television shows, which was devoted to fishing, hunting and the out-of-doors.","title":"Ralph W. 'Bud' Leavitt Jr."}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Leavitt's stature within the state was such that columnist Roy Blount Jr. wrote of the Maine sportswriter that he \"fishes with Ted Williams and Red Smith – or, rather, they trout-fish with him.\"","title":"Ralph W. 'Bud' Leavitt Jr."}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" An early conservationist and son of a paper mill union leader, Leavitt urged the state of Maine to acquire lands for public use; one such preserve is today named for the sportswriter and television personality.","title":"Ralph W. 'Bud' Leavitt Jr."}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mildred Brown \"Brownie\" Schrumpf (January 24, 1903 – March 2, 2001) was an American home economist, food educator, and author.","title":"Mildred Brown Schrumpf"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Named the \"Unofficial Ambassador of Good Eating\" by the Maine Department of Agriculture, she wrote a weekly food column for the \"Bangor Daily News\" from 1951 to 1994 promoting traditional Maine recipes.","title":"Mildred Brown Schrumpf"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" She was the main proponent of the claim that the chocolate brownie was invented in Bangor.","title":"Mildred Brown Schrumpf"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" She was inducted into the Maine Women's Hall of Fame in 1997.","title":"Mildred Brown Schrumpf"}
