Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Trained at L’Ecole des Beaux-Arts in Paris, he designed virtually every type of Victorian structure—cottages, mansions, townhouses, apartment houses, hotels, tenements, banks, stores, churches, schools, libraries, offices, factories, railroad stations, and a museum.","title":"Detlef Lienau"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Lienau was recognized by clients and colleagues alike as one of the most creative and technically proficient architects of the period, and was one of the 29 founding members of the American Institute of Architects.","title":"Detlef Lienau"}
