Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"\"All About Lisa\" is the twentieth episode and season finale of \"The Simpsons\"<nowiki>'</nowiki> nineteenth season.","title":"All About Lisa"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It originally aired on the Fox network in the United States on May 18, 2008.","title":"All About Lisa"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Lisa Simpson becomes Krusty the Clown's newest assistant and steals his spotlight.","title":"All About Lisa"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" She wins Entertainer of the Year at the Springfield Media awards, but is warned that with her sudden fame comes a new attitude towards others and herself.","title":"All About Lisa"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Meanwhile, Homer and Bart bond over their newfound love of coin collecting.","title":"All About Lisa"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The episode features narration by Sideshow Mel.","title":"All About Lisa"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" It was written by John Frink and directed by Steven Dean Moore.","title":"All About Lisa"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" Drew Carey guest voices as himself, appearing as a guest on Krusty's show.","title":"All About Lisa"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mike B. Anderson (born 1973), sometimes credited as Mikel B. Anderson, is an American television director who works on \"The Simpsons\" and has directed numerous episodes of the show, and was animated in \"The Secret War of Lisa Simpson\" as cadet Anderson.","title":"Mike B. Anderson"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" While a college student, he directed the live action feature films \"Alone in the T-Shirt Zone\" (1986) and \"Kamillions\" (1989).","title":"Mike B. Anderson"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Since 1990, he has worked primarily in animation including being a consulting producer on the series, \"The Oblongs\", and story consultant on \"Tripping the Rift\".","title":"Mike B. Anderson"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"\"Lisa Goes Gaga\" is the twenty-second and final episode of the twenty-third season of the American animated sitcom \"The Simpsons\".","title":"Lisa Goes Gaga"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It originally aired on the Fox network in the United States on May 20, 2012.","title":"Lisa Goes Gaga"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" In the episode, American singer-songwriter Lady Gaga makes a visit to Springfield, where all of its residents are in a state of depression.","title":"Lisa Goes Gaga"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Main character Lisa Simpson is arguably the most depressed person in the city, prompting Gaga to go out of her way to teach Lisa the meaning of happiness.","title":"Lisa Goes Gaga"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lisette Dufour (Born 1949) is a Québécoise voice actress who is better known as the French voice of Lisa Simpson on \"The Simpsons\".","title":"Lisette Dufour"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lisa Marie Simpson is a fictional character in the animated television series \"The Simpsons\".","title":"Lisa Simpson"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" She is the middle child and most intelligent of the Simpson family.","title":"Lisa Simpson"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Voiced by Yeardley Smith, Lisa first appeared on television in \"The Tracey Ullman Show\" short \"Good Night\" on April 19, 1987.","title":"Lisa Simpson"}
