Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lotion Play is a subset of the better known Wet-And-Messy fetish (WAM), which typically involves participants using food (such as pudding or whipped cream), mud, or paint as a lubricant to facilitate sexual activity.","title":"Lotion play"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Lotion Play isolates lotion specifically as a lubricating medium - setting it apart in the Wet-and-Messy genre, as other common WAM mediums do not have such specific popularity as Lotion Play.","title":"Lotion play"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Lotion Play (ローションプレイ , rōshon purei ) , also known as gookkake, gluekkake, is a popular fetish, form of Japanese erotica and prostitution request involving the use of copious amounts of lubricant, which in the Japanese language is referred to by the Old-French word \"lotion\" (ローション in Japanese).","title":"Lotion play"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":"Typically lotion play involves a participant rubbing lotion on another using their body, sexual intercourse in a pool or bath filled with lotion, or lotion being poured over the participants during sex.","title":"Lotion play"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" In Japan (and other parts of the world), lotion is available in concentrated form (e.g.: liter/gallon) which can be added to hot water to produce the desired amount of lotion.","title":"Lotion play"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" A 1-gallon concentrate will typically yield 6-10 gallons of lotion (J-Lube Lotion Concentrate).","title":"Lotion play"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" The main component in most lotion is polyacrylate.","title":"Lotion play"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" A similar effect can be achieved by dissolving powdered methyl cellulose in water.","title":"Lotion play"}
