Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Manta is a steel family launched roller coaster at SeaWorld San Diego in San Diego, California, United States.","title":"Manta (SeaWorld San Diego)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The ride was manufactured by MACK Rides and opened to the public on May 26, 2012.","title":"Manta (SeaWorld San Diego)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" It utilizes the same ride system that was used in Blue Fire which opened in 2009 at Europa Park.","title":"Manta (SeaWorld San Diego)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Millennium Force is a steel roller coaster built by Intamin at Cedar Point amusement park in Sandusky, Ohio, United States.","title":"Millennium Force"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was the fourteenth roller coaster to be built at the park since Blue Streak opened in 1964.","title":"Millennium Force"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Upon completion in 2000, Millennium Force broke six world records and was the world's first Giga Coaster, a roller coaster that exceeds 300 ft in height and completes a full circuit.","title":"Millennium Force"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" It was briefly the tallest and fastest in the world until Steel Dragon 2000 opened later the same year.","title":"Millennium Force"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The ride is also the third-longest roller coaster in North America after The Beast at Kings Island and Fury 325 at Carowinds.","title":"Millennium Force"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" It was the first roller coaster to use a cable lift system rather than a traditional chain lift.","title":"Millennium Force"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" The coaster has a 310 ft , 45-degree lift hill with a 300 ft drop and features two tunnels, three overbanked turns, and four hills.","title":"Millennium Force"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" It has a top speed of 93 mph .","title":"Millennium Force"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Blue Fire is a launched roller coaster at Europa-Park.","title":"Blue Fire"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The coaster opened in 2009 as part of a new Iceland-themed expansion to Europa-Park.","title":"Blue Fire"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" As the first launched coaster built by MACK Rides, Blue Fire will serve as the park's tenth roller coaster and their first roller coaster with inversions.","title":"Blue Fire"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The ride's tagline is \"Discover Pure Energy\".","title":"Blue Fire"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Leviathan is a steel roller coaster in the Medieval Faire section of the park at Canada's Wonderland in Vaughan, Ontario, Canada.","title":"Leviathan (roller coaster)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is the first roller coaster designed by Swiss firm Bolliger & Mabillard to exceed a height of 300 ft , putting it in a class of roller coasters commonly referred to as \"giga\".","title":"Leviathan (roller coaster)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" At 5486 ft long, 306 ft tall, and with a top speed of 92 mph , Leviathan is the tallest and fastest roller coaster in Canada.","title":"Leviathan (roller coaster)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" s of 2015 , Leviathan is ranked as the eighth-tallest, and the eighth-fastest roller coaster in the world, and the third-tallest traditional lift-style coaster in the world.","title":"Leviathan (roller coaster)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" It was the 16th roller coaster to be built at Canada's Wonderland, and the ride's track was completed in February 2012, with the first test run being completed on 15 March 2012.","title":"Leviathan (roller coaster)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The coaster opened to season pass holders on 27 April 2012, and to the general public on 6 May 2012.","title":"Leviathan (roller coaster)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Top Thrill Dragster is a steel accelerator roller coaster built by Intamin at Cedar Point in Sandusky, Ohio, United States.","title":"Top Thrill Dragster"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was the sixteenth roller coaster built at the park since the Blue Streak in 1964.","title":"Top Thrill Dragster"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" When built in 2003, it was the first full circuit roller coaster to exceed 400 ft in height, and was the tallest roller coaster in the world, before being surpassed by Kingda Ka at Six Flags Great Adventure in May 2005.","title":"Top Thrill Dragster"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Top Thrill Dragster, along with Kingda Ka, are the only strata coasters in existence.","title":"Top Thrill Dragster"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" It was the second hydraulically launched roller coaster built by Intamin, following \"Xcelerator\" at Knott's Berry Farm.","title":"Top Thrill Dragster"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" The tagline for Top Thrill Dragster is \"Race for the Sky\".","title":"Top Thrill Dragster"}
