Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"On the afternoon of 18 January 2017, a major avalanche occurred on Gran Sasso d'Italia, a mountain in Rigopiano, a tourist destination in the province of Pescara, in Southern Italy's Abruzzo region.","title":"Rigopiano avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The avalanche struck the luxury resort Hotel Rigopiano, killing twenty-nine people and injuring eleven others.","title":"Rigopiano avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The avalanche is the deadliest in Italy since the White Friday avalanches in 1916, and the deadliest avalanche in Europe since the Galtür avalanche in 1999.","title":"Rigopiano avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The MYH16 gene encodes a protein called myosin heavy chain 16 which is a muscle protein in mammals.","title":"MYH16 gene"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" At least in primates, it is a specialized muscle protein found only in the temporalis and masseter muscles of the jaw.","title":"MYH16 gene"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Myosin heavy chain proteins are important in muscle contraction, and if they are missing, the muscles will be smaller.","title":"MYH16 gene"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" In non-human primates, MYH16 is functional and the animals have powerful jaw muscles.","title":"MYH16 gene"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" In humans, the MYH16 gene has a mutation which causes the protein not to function.","title":"MYH16 gene"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Although the exact importance of this change in accounting for differences between humans and other apes is not yet clear, such a change may be related to increased brain size and finer control of the jaw which facilitates speech.","title":"MYH16 gene"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" It is not clear how the MYH16 mutation relates to other changes to the jaw and skull in early human evolution (for example, whether the MYH16 mutation happened first and led to other changes, or whether the MYH16 mutation happened after other changes made the MYH16 protein no longer necessary).","title":"MYH16 gene"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Galtür avalanche occurred on 23 February 1999 in the Alpine village of Galtür, Austria.","title":"1999 Galtür avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It took less than 60 seconds to hit Galtür.","title":"1999 Galtür avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" At 50 m high and traveling at 290 km/h , this powder avalanche hit with great force, overturning cars, ruining buildings and burying 57 people.","title":"1999 Galtür avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" By the time rescue crews managed to arrive, 31 people – locals and tourists – had died.","title":"1999 Galtür avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" This avalanche was considered the worst Alpine avalanche in 40 years.","title":"1999 Galtür avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" Three major weather systems originating from the Atlantic accounted for large snowfalls totaling around four meters in the area.","title":"1999 Galtür avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" Freeze-thaw conditions created a weak layer on top of an existing snow pack; further snow was then deposited on top.","title":"1999 Galtür avalanche"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":7,"text":" This, coupled with high wind speeds, created large snow drifts and caused roughly 170,000 tons of snow to be deposited.","title":"1999 Galtür avalanche"}
