Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"In Renaissance London, playing company was the usual term for a company of actors.","title":"Playing company"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" These companies were organized around a group of ten or so shareholders (or \"sharers\"), who performed in the plays but were also responsible for management.","title":"Playing company"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The sharers employed \"hired men\" that is, the minor actors and the workers behind the scenes.","title":"Playing company"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The major companies were based at specific theatres in London; the most successful of them, William Shakespeare's company the King's Men, had the open-air Globe Theatre for summer seasons and the enclosed Blackfriars Theatre in the winters.","title":"Playing company"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" The Admiral's Men occupied the Rose Theatre in the 1590s, and the Fortune Theatre in the early 17th century.","title":"Playing company"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Admiral's Men (also called the Admiral's company, more strictly, the Earl of Nottingham's Men; after 1603, Prince Henry's Men; after 1612, the Elector Palatine's Men or the Palsgrave's Men) was a playing company or troupe of actors in the Elizabethan and Stuart eras.","title":"Admiral's Men"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is generally considered the second most important acting troupe of English Renaissance theatre (after the company of Shakespeare, the Lord Chamberlain's or King's Men).","title":"Admiral's Men"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 2011 Hotan attack was a bomb-and-knife attack that occurred in Hotan, Xinjiang, China on July 18, 2011.","title":"2011 Hotan attack"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" According to witnesses, the assailants were a group of 18 young Uyghur men who opposed the local government's campaign against the full-face Islamic veil, which had grown popular among older Hotan women in 2009 but were also used in a series of violent crimes.","title":"2011 Hotan attack"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The men occupied a police station on Nuerbage Street at noon, killing two security guards with knives and bombs and taking eight hostages.","title":"2011 Hotan attack"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The attackers then yelled religious slogans, including ones associated with Jihadism, as they replaced the Chinese flag on top of a police station with another flag, the identity of which is disputed.","title":"2011 Hotan attack"}
