Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Crimson King, known to some as Los' or Ram Abbalah, is a fictional character created by Stephen King.","title":"Crimson King"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is the primary antagonist of King's eight-volume \"Dark Tower\" series, as well as the novels \"Insomnia\" and \"Black House\".","title":"Crimson King"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Described as \"Gan's crazy side\", the Crimson King is the ultimate ruler of the Red (also called the Random and the Outer Dark), and the archetypal embodiment of evil in Stephen King's fictional multiverse.","title":"Crimson King"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" His goal is to topple the Dark Tower which serves as the linchpin of time and space, destroying the multitude of universes which revolve around it so that he can rule in the primordial chaos which follows.","title":"Crimson King"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"All-World is a fictional location in Stephen King's \"The Dark Tower\" series of novels.","title":"All-World"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" All-World is the world known to contain the \"Keystone Tower\" in the Dark Tower series.","title":"All-World"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is the only world that contains the Dark Tower in its physical form; all others contain a representative of the Tower, such as a rose.","title":"All-World"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" From All-World, it is possible to actually enter the Dark Tower.","title":"All-World"}
