Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The UK Classical Charts are three record charts based on classical music in the United Kingdom: the Classical Artist Albums Chart, the Classical Compilation Albums Chart and the Specialist Classical Albums Chart.","title":"UK Classical Charts"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The charts are commercial monitoring and marketing devices used by the UK music industry to measure its effectiveness in promoting and selling albums, nominally in the field of classical music.","title":"UK Classical Charts"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" All three charts are compiled by the Official Charts Company (OCC).","title":"UK Classical Charts"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The measurements are made by collating the returns of sales from a number of well-known music stores (high street and online stores) on a regular basis, and this enables a ranking to be established.","title":"UK Classical Charts"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Most classical artist album sales in the UK are from crossover artists.","title":"UK Classical Charts"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" For an album to be classified as classical in the charts, it has to have 60% of the playing time dedicated to \"classical or traditional music\".","title":"UK Classical Charts"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" Only albums that entirely classical or traditional music qualify for inclusion in the Specialist Classical Albums Chart.","title":"UK Classical Charts"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"KFAC was a commercial classical music radio station in Los Angeles, broadcasting for most of its life on 1330 kHz AM, and subsequently in both simulcast and separate programming on 92.3 MHz FM as well.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" \"Only 41 of nearly 9,000 commercial radio stations in the United States play classical music\" and KFAC was considered one of the best.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" On September 20, 1989 at 2 p.m., new owners changed both its name and its format, depriving Southern California of a major cultural institution.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" During its heyday, the station was arguably the most important cultural organization in the Los Angeles area, having greater influence on lovers of classical music than even the Los Angeles Philharmonic.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" Announcers such as John Conte, Howard Rhines, Dick Crawford, Thomas Cassidy, Carl Princi, Fred Crane, Steve Allen, Alfred Leonard, Tom Dixon, Bill Carlson, Dick Joy, Tom Franklin, Ed Stoddard, Bernie Alan, Rodger Layng, John Santana, Steve Markham and Doug Ordunio were featured on the station.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":5,"text":" For several years, the station also carried the daily syndicated \"Adventures in Good Music\" with Karl Haas.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":6,"text":" Other regularly scheduled programs were hosted by Leonora Schildkraut, Werner Klemperer, and Gussie Moran.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Women in music describes the role of women as composers, songwriters, instrumental performers, singers, conductors, music scholars, music educators, music critics/music journalists and other musical professions.","title":"Women in music"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" As well, it describes music movements (e.g., women's music, which is music written and performed by women for women), events and genres related to women, women's issues and feminism.","title":"Women in music"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" In the 2010s, while women comprise a significant proportion of popular music and classical music singers, and a significant proportion of songwriters (many of them being singer-songwriters), there are few women record producers, rock critics and rock instrumentalists.","title":"Women in music"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Notable women artists in pop, such as Bjork and Lady Gaga have commented about sexism and gender discrimination in the music industry.","title":"Women in music"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":4,"text":" In classical music, although there have been a huge number of women composers from the Medieval period to the present day, women composers are significantly underrepresented in the commonly performed classical music repertoire, music history textbooks and music encyclopedias; for example, in the \"Concise Oxford History of Music\", Clara Schumann is one of the only female composers who is mentioned.","title":"Women in music"}
