Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Sinclair is an unincorporated community in Preston County, West Virginia, located at the intersection of Davis Hill Road and Sinclair Coalbank Road.","title":"Sinclair, West Virginia"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The town is named after oil drilling in the area performed by Sinclair Oil Corp. The Sinclair United Methodist Church is also located in Sinclair, West Virginia.","title":"Sinclair, West Virginia"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Sinclair Oil Corporation is an American petroleum corporation, founded by Harry F. Sinclair on May 1, 1916, as the Sinclair Oil and Refining Corporation by combining the assets of 11 small petroleum companies.","title":"Sinclair Oil Corporation"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" Originally a New York corporation, Sinclair Oil reincorporated in Wyoming in 1976.","title":"Sinclair Oil Corporation"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" The corporation's logo features the silhouette of a large green dinosaur.","title":"Sinclair Oil Corporation"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Harry Ford Sinclair (July 6, 1876 in Benwood, West Virginia - November 10, 1956 in Pasadena, California) was an American industrialist, founder of Sinclair Oil.","title":"Harry Ford Sinclair"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was implicated in the 1920s Teapot Dome Scandal, and served six months in prison for jury tampering.","title":"Harry Ford Sinclair"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" Afterwards he returned to his former life and enjoyed its prosperity until his death.","title":"Harry Ford Sinclair"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The R.E. Hoy No. 1 Oil Well was constructed by the Sinclair Oil & Refining Corporation in September 1916.","title":"R. E. Hoy No. 1 Oil Well"}
